            stem: "A state statute requires a sentence of life imprisonment without the possibility of parole for anyone convicted of first-degree murder, and gives the sentencing judge no discretion. A defendant who was fifteen when he committed a first-degree murder is convicted as an adult and sentenced under the statute. He challenges the sentence.",
