            say: "Most constitutional errors reverse unless harmless beyond a reasonable doubt; structural errors always reverse; unpreserved errors get plain-error review.",
            elements: ["Preserved constitutional error: the state must show it harmless beyond a reasonable doubt (Chapman)", "Structural error: automatic reversal, with no harmlessness inquiry", "Unpreserved error: plain-error review"],
